      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I just had this issue with a PC Medium avatar being shown as Poor on the server side.\n\nI found that I had an object which had it's mesh removed, but it still had 2 materials on it. It seems like the materials were still being counted during the server checks, but not in Unity or in-game.\n\nBefore doing some material and mesh changes, \"materialSlotsUsed\" was up to 17 (\"materialCount\" was below this), and my uneducated guess would be that this caused it to show as Poor.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-06T11:33:40.848Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Title already says it all. Yesterday, multiple people told me that they couldn't see my avatar because it was perf blocked as Very Poor, even though it should be Poor instead. Manually showing the avatar and then going back to the \"shield\" setting fixed it, but that's obviously not a solution.\n\nI don't want to post the full avatar ID in this public forum, but I can of course give it out if requested (it starts with ebcc58de if any dev is looking at the avis on my account).",
